<===> README.md
A selector ending with an escaped space (`.a\ `) lost the space of the
following descendant combinator, so `.a\  .b` was emitted as `.a\ .b`,
which means something else. `compound` and `escaped_backslash` (`.a\\ .b`)
are controls. Expected output generated with dart-sass 1.93.1.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> child/input.scss
.a\ > .b {x: y}
<===> child/output.css
.a\  > .b {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> compound/input.scss
.a\ .b {x: y}
<===> compound/output.css
.a\ .b {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> descendant/input.scss
.a\  .b {x: y}
<===> descendant/output.css
.a\  .b {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> escaped_backslash/input.scss
.a\\ .b {x: y}
.c\\\  .d {x: y}
<===> escaped_backslash/output.css
.a\\ .b {
  x: y;
}

.c\\\  .d {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> nested/input.scss
.a\  {
  .b {x: y}
  & .c {x: y}
  &.d {x: y}
}
<===> nested/output.css
.a\  .b {
  x: y;
}
.a\  .c {
  x: y;
}
.a\ .d {
  x: y;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parent_list/input.scss
div sp\ ,#abcan {
  p, |q {x: y}
}
<===> parent_list/output.css
div sp\  p, div sp\  |q, #abcan p, #abcan |q {
  x: y;
}
